      "suggestedVersionCode": "5",
      "description": "Battery Monitor shows Android's per-app charge estimates, available\nforeground/background estimates, wakelocks and the system battery timeline.\nIt keeps validated usage history on your device, without ads, accounts or\ntelemetry. Android 14 or later is required.\nNetwork permission is used only for temporary ADB setup on this device.\n\nGuided on-device ADB setup grants diagnostic permissions without a computer\nor separate Shizuku installation. Keep Android Settings and the app visible\nin split screen while pairing. ADB disconnects after setup; Wireless debugging\ncan then be turned off. Computer ADB and Shizuku remain alternatives.\n\nThis early public beta is an independent GPLv3-or-later Wattdog fork;\nestimates and physical-device\nbehavior still need validation. Uninstalling removes saved history.\n\nSetup and limitations: https://github.com/Sivivatu/battery-monitor#install-and-enable-collection\n",
      "issueTracker": "https://github.com/Sivivatu/battery-monitor/issues",
      "license": "GPL-3.0-or-later",
      "name": "Battery Monitor",
      "sourceCode": "https://github.com/Sivivatu/battery-monitor",
      "summary": "Local battery estimates and app usage history",
      "webSite": "https://github.com/Sivivatu/battery-monitor",
      "added": 1793312484000,
      "packageName": "io.github.sivivatu.batterymonitor",
      "lastUpdated": 1793788243000,
      "localized": {
        "en-US": {
          "whatsNew": "On-device ADB setup without a computer or Shizuku. Keep Settings and the app in split screen while pairing.\nInline port validation and clearer setup errors.\nDirect collection continues after Wireless debugging is turned off.\nFix parsing of fractional battery-discharge counters.\nPrevent missed ADB notifications during fast permission grants.\n"
        }
      }
    }
